    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d245">

                <pb facs="0249" n="237" sameAs="frus:frus1941v01/pg237"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">760C.61/966a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Ambassador to the
                        Polish Government in Exile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Biddle</hi>), <hi
                        rendition="#italic">at London</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-06-26T16:00:00-04:00">June 26, 1941—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Polish Series No. 14. We have received press reports to the effect that the
                    Polish Government has made certain approaches to the Soviet Government. Any
                    information which you may be able to furnish the Department regarding the nature
                    of these approaches, the circumstances in which they were made, and the
                    character of any reply which may have been received, would be appreciated.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
